[{:adr/authoritative_for ["90-docs/design-quality/design-quality.datoms.edn を design-quality スコアリングの schema/catalog 正本とする位置づけ（DataScript/Datomic transactable EDN）" "90-docs/design-quality/design-quality-ledger.edn を append-only スコアイベント台帳の正本とする位置づけ（手編集禁止、追記のみ）" ".claude/workflows/design-quality-score.js を再実行可能な正本ワークフローとする位置づけ" "新規に design-quality/UI品質数値化の仕組みを作る前に、この ADR と 90-docs/design-quality/ の既存ledgerを必ず確認する、という再発防止規則（BMC/Lean Loop と同型の教訓）"], :adr/addendum-2026-07-13 "Co-Scientist kaizen pass (isekai.ux ADR-0007 移植, keiei-arbor-coscientist-engine\n  ADR-2606141500 が原典). Added deterministic fitness function\n  90-docs/design-quality/audit.cljc (isekai.ux.audit port, no LLM/browser, 9 axes) +\n  90-docs/design-quality/coscientist.cljc (isekai.ux.coscientist port, offline/heuristic\n  Generate->Reflect->Rank(Elo)->Evolve->Meta, no langchain-clj dep). Iteration 01\n  (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-01.edn): baseline 71.55/100 across the 4\n  sample pages -- the SAME libraries the 3-judge llm-judge panel scored 4.0-5.0/5 on every\n  HIG axis, yet no judge flagged any of: missing min-height>=44px on\n  .liquid-glass__button/.liquid-glass__icon-button (tap-targets w=0.13), no dvh fallback on\n  .kotoba-shell__app (dynamic-viewport w=0.09), only bottom safe-area-inset covered not top\n  (safe-area w=0.13), no <meta theme-color> (color-scheme w=0.06), no viewport-fit=cover\n  (viewport w=0.10), no max-width media query on the liquid-glass-ui showcase (responsive\n  w=0.07, that page only). Elo-ranked (predicted-gain is the judge, no LLM debate), shipped\n  the 4 consumer-fixable low-risk findings as unlayered app CSS batch\n  design-quality-kaizen-1 via generate-samples.cljs's :head opt (no shared orgs/kotoba-lang/*\n  checkout edited). Re-measured: 71.55 -> 90.38/100 (+18.83; the 3 shipped samples each\n  71.14->96.25, the untouched liquid-glass-ui showcase page stayed flat at 72.77 as the\n  control proving the delta is real). viewport (kotoba-ui.shell/page hardcodes a single\n  meta tag with no :head override point) and responsive (needs editing the showcase page\n  itself) were deferred as upstream-only follow-ups in iteration 01.\n\n  Iteration 02 (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-02.edn) landed both deferred\n  findings for real via isolated git worktrees outside the superproject (kotoba-ui and\n  liquid-glass-ui each), verified against each repo's own test suite (20 tests/130\n  assertions; 59 tests/632 assertions, both green) before pushing, merged server-side\n  (gh api .../merges, no local rebase/force-push), manifest/west.yml pins advanced via\n  nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry <name> (minimal per-entry diff, verified,\n  no wholesale regen). This round caught a REAL bug in the loop itself before shipping:\n  heuristic-hypothesis's fix text is generic per-axis and doesn't verify the proposed\n  CSS selector exists on the actual target page -- it proposed\n  .kotoba-shell__app{min-height:100dvh} for the liquid-glass-ui showcase page, which\n  doesn't use kotoba-ui.shell at all (grep -c kotoba-shell__app docs/index.html == 0);\n  shipping it as-worded would have been a dead no-op fix. Caught by checking the real\n  markup before shipping, then applying the correct selectors (body, and the page's\n  actually-present .liquid-glass__nav-bar). Final measured state after 3 audit rounds:\n  71.55 -> 90.38 -> 95.16 -> 100.00/100, 0 findings across all 4 pages (converged on the\n  current 9-axis rubric). Added a converged-state branch to coscientist.cljc's\n  iteration-md (isekai's own iteration-07 pattern) so future re-runs at 0 findings report\n  honestly instead of rendering empty tables. Iteration 03 seed: fix\n  heuristic-hypothesis to verify selectors against real page content, add a WCAG 1.4.3\n  contrast-ratio axis, wire a real screenshot-critic lens into Generate, consider\n  promoting the nav-bar safe-area-top fix from demo-page-only into liquid-glass.style\n  itself.", :adr/addendum-2026-07-13b "Extended scoring to kotoba-lang/kami-studio + kotoba-lang/kami-creative-studio (user\n  asked for 'kotoba-studio'/'kotoba-creative-studio', which do not exist -- gh repo list\n  confirmed only kami-studio/kami-creative-studio exist; both were already manually\n  cloned under orgs/kotoba-lang/ but unregistered in west.yml/repos.edn). Neither uses\n  kotoba-ui/liquid-glass-ui/uikit/appkit at all (kami-studio: kotoba-lang/html+css only;\n  kami-creative-studio: reagent+shadow-cljs+kotoba-lang/kisekae+model-viewer), so the\n  :lint layer doesn't apply. Added :audit layer (9 axes, design-quality.audit,\n  deterministic) to the catalog for the first time (previously only used ad-hoc via\n  coscientist.cljc, never fed into the ledger) + 2 new :lib entries + an adapted\n  3-judge :llm-judge panel (consistency axis redefined as internal self-consistency,\n  no sibling-family comparison). Results: kami-studio audit 50.75/100, judges clarity\n  4.07/deference 4.33/depth 3.23/consistency 4.57/token-discipline 3.00 (n=3).\n  kami-creative-studio audit 67.72/100, judges clarity 4.00/deference 4.00/depth\n  3.50/consistency 4.00/token-discipline 3.00 (n=2, 1 judge failed structured-output\n  retry). Cross-signal finding: token_discipline scored 3.00/5 on BOTH apps (vs\n  4.5-4.93 for the kotoba-ui-family libraries) and the audit's color-scheme axis\n  independently flags both as missing theme-color/color-scheme -- two independent\n  measurement layers agree these apps lack any token/CSS-variable layer, pointing at\n  adopting kotoba-ui.theme/shitsuke.tokens as the highest-leverage improvement for\n  both. 30 ledger lines appended (18 audit + 10 llm-judge-mean; raw per-judge scores\n  were not preserved by this round's workflow design, mean-only -- a gap vs the\n  original 4-library workflow's full traceability, noted as a process improvement for\n  next time). Formal west.yml/repos.edn registration of these 2 repos is out of scope\n  for this scoring-only pass.", :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-ui-design-system", :adr/related ["adr-2607022800-kotoba-lang-default-uiux-appkit-uikit-interface-fundamentals" "com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/uikit" "com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/appkit" "com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-ui" "com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/liquid-glass-ui" "com-junkawasaki/orgs/kotoba-lang/shitsuke"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607132300-kotoba-lang-uiux-design-quality-scoring", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/addendum-2026-07-13d "Fixed the audit-tooling bug addendum-c found, rather than auditing another page\n  (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/iteration-04.edn). Added score-site to\n  90-docs/design-quality/audit.cljc: takes a page's parts ({:html ... :css\n  string-or-vector :js ...}) instead of one pre-assembled string, detects\n  <link rel=stylesheet href=...> in the HTML via external-stylesheet-hrefs (handles\n  quoted and bare attribute values), and sets :incomplete? true + a :warning naming the\n  unaccounted-for hrefs when no :css was supplied to cover them -- so the exact\n  addendum-c mistake (scoring kami-creative-studio's index.html alone, silently missing\n  its external public/css/ui.css) is now caught by the tool itself instead of requiring\n  a human to notice. score-page (single-string) is unchanged and used internally after\n  assembly; audit now calls score-site per page (existing plain-string callers are\n  unaffected) and surfaces a top-level :incomplete list of any flagged page names.\n  Regression-checked: grepped every previously-audited file for external stylesheets\n  BEFORE touching code -- none of the 5 prior 100/100 pages (4 samples + kami-studio)\n  use one, so those scores were never at risk from this bug class. Reproduced the exact\n  addendum-c bug as a test case (score-site without :css -> 67.72/incomplete?=true/\n  warning naming css/ui.css; with :css -> 66.59/incomplete?=nil), confirming the fix\n  catches what previously required manual discovery. Separately (not a bug in this\n  fix): re-running a full 6-page convergence check initially showed kami-creative-studio\n  regressed to 5 findings -- root cause was the superproject's shared checkout at\n  orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-creative-studio/public/ being gitignored build output never\n  rebuilt there since addendum-c's fix landed (the fix build+verify+audit all happened\n  inside the now-deleted isolated worktree). Confirmed the fix really is on main (commit\n  966d445, merge 7c0439e) and rebuilt public/ in the shared checkout (shadow-cljs\n  release + pages build) to get a fresh, accurate reading -- not a regression, but a\n  reminder that gitignored build artifacts in a shared checkout silently go stale.\n  Final state: all 6 pages this system has ever audited (4 samples, kami-studio,\n  kami-creative-studio via the corrected score-site path) = 100.00/100, 0 findings,\n  :incomplete? correctly nil on every one.", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-13", :adr/library-scores-2026-07-13 "[{:consistency 5, :dark-mode 0, :lib :uikit, :depth 4, :token-compliance 1, :deference 4.43, :token-discipline 4.5, :single-entry 1, :clarity 4.73} {:consistency 5, :dark-mode 0, :lib :appkit, :depth 3.6, :token-compliance 1, :deference 4.63, :token-discipline 4.5, :single-entry 1, :clarity 4.77} {:consistency 4.75, :dark-mode 1, :note \"clarity/deference/depth/consistency/token-discipline は judge 3体中1体が StructuredOutput retry cap 超過で失敗したため n=2 で集計\", :lib :kotoba-ui, :depth 3.75, :token-compliance 0.91, :deference 4.15, :token-discipline 4.6, :single-entry 1, :clarity 4.5} {:consistency 4.03, :dark-mode 1, :deference-stdev 0.5, :note \"deference軸のjudge間disagreementが顕著（2.8〜4.0）— デフォルトのglass装飾がcontent優先かchrome先行か判断が割れた\", :lib :liquid-glass-ui, :depth 4.97, :token-compliance 0.71, :deference 3.33, :token-discipline 4.93, :single-entry \"該当なし（leaf layer）\", :clarity 4.57}]", :adr/addendum-2026-07-13c "Kaizen pass on kami-studio + kami-creative-studio (90-docs/design-quality/coscientist/\n  iteration-03.md), landing the addendum-b findings for real. Before shipping, found a\n  SECOND real audit-methodology bug: kami-creative-studio's actual CSS lives in a\n  separately-linked public/css/ui.css, not inlined in public/index.html -- audit.cljc's\n  score-page takes one string, so the addendum-b run (index.html alone) never saw the\n  real styling. Concatenating index.html+ui.css gave a corrected baseline of 66.59/100\n  (not 67.72) with a materially different finding set (overflow-guard/responsive were\n  false negatives; reduced-motion was a newly-surfaced real gap). Also found: this app\n  is client-side-rendered, so tap-targets/focus-visible's <button>/<input> literal-tag\n  regex structurally false-positives (matches nothing in static files since all markup\n  is JS-generated at runtime) -- verified by hand-grepping ui.cljs instead of trusting\n  the tool: tap-targets was genuinely fine ($button already had min-height:44px) but\n  focus-visible was a REAL unmeasured gap (only $input had :focus, not :focus-visible;\n  $button/$trait-card/$file had none). Documented as a standing limitation of\n  design-quality.audit for CSR apps, not fixed this pass. Shipped via isolated git\n  worktrees (kami-studio 83edddf->c6143d6, no test suite, verified via re-render+\n  re-audit; kami-creative-studio 6fc4a1c->7c0439e, existing 6 tests/23 assertions green,\n  full local build via npm install + shadow-cljs release (0 warnings) + pages build,\n  confirmed the compiled CSS actually contains every fix before re-auditing), merged\n  server-side, worktrees/branches cleaned up. Results: kami-studio 50.75->100.00/100 (7\n  findings fixed: viewport-fit, safe-area all 4 edges, focus-visible, theme-color+\n  color-scheme, overflow-x guard, responsive breakpoint, html lang -- also reformatted\n  the 1-line source into readable multi-line hiccup, no functional change).\n  kami-creative-studio 66.59->100.00/100 (viewport-fit, color-scheme, safe-area on both\n  fixed top/bottom bars, the real focus-visible gap found by hand, a hand-written global\n  prefers-reduced-motion reset since shadow-css's per-class @media syntax can't express\n  a universal-selector rule). One honest documented limitation: kami-creative-studio's\n  $top safe-area-inset-top padding grows the header box outward (content-box, no global\n  border-box reset) rather than clipping content, but $workspace's calc(100vh - 54px)\n  doesn't account for the extra height, so a notched device could clip a few dozen px off\n  the workspace grid's bottom -- follow-up noted, not silently claimed as perfect. west.yml\n  registration remains out of scope; both fixes are landed on each repo's own main\n  regardless of manifest status. 20 more ledger lines appended (10 audit rows per app, all\n  1.0, design-quality-studios-kaizen-20260713-0942 run).", :adr/body "# ADR-2607132300: kotoba-lang design-system UI/UX 品質を EDN で数値化する design-quality-score システムを導入する\n\n**Status**: accepted — 実装済み・初回スコアリング実行済み（2026-07-13）。\n\n本文は同名 .md ファイル参照（Context / Decision / Findings / Limitations / Consequences / Alternatives Considered / References の各節）。", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/scope-boundary "本ADRは uikit/appkit/kotoba-ui/liquid-glass-ui の4ライブラリの design-quality スコアリング（lint層+llm-judge層+sample-visual層）と、そのEDN保存形式・再実行可能ワークフロー・サンプルページ生成の仕組みを扱う。Lighthouse/axe-core/実contrast計算・3-judge visual panel化は follow-up としてスコープ外。", :adr/date "2026-07-13", :adr/methodology "[{:layer :lint, :scale \"0-1\", :method \"grepベースの決定論的実測（agent+Bash、推測値不使用）\", :axes [:axis/token-compliance :axis/dark-mode-coverage :axis/single-entry-discipline]} {:layer :llm-judge, :scale \"1-5\", :method \"3体の独立judgeが実ソース+docsを読んで採点、平均+標準偏差を記録\", :axes [:axis/clarity :axis/deference :axis/depth :axis/consistency :axis/token-discipline-judged]} {:layer :sample-visual, :scale \"1-5\", :method \"オーケストレータ単発視認（3-judge panelではない、hero/nav部分のみ視認、follow-upで拡張予定）\", :axes [:axis/clarity :axis/deference :axis/depth :axis/consistency :axis/token-discipline-judged]}]", :db/id -1, :adr/sample-ranking-2026-07-13 "[{:rank 1, :sample :appkit-desktop-sample, :visual-mean 4.28, :libs [:appkit :kotoba-ui :liquid-glass-ui]} {:rank 2, :sample :uikit-mobile-sample, :visual-mean 4.26, :libs [:uikit :kotoba-ui :liquid-glass-ui]} {:rank 3, :sample :kotoba-ui-bare-sample, :visual-mean 4.2, :libs [:kotoba-ui :liquid-glass-ui]} {:rank 4, :sample :liquid-glass-ui-showcase, :visual-mean 4.1, :libs [:liquid-glass-ui], :file \"orgs/kotoba-lang/liquid-glass-ui/docs/index.html\", :note \"既存showcase、kotoba-ui.theme非経由。deference軸2.5が最下位の主因（意図的なkitchen-sinkデモのため）、depth軸は5.0で全サンプル中最高\"}]", :adr/limitations ["Lighthouse/axe-core/WCAG contrast の実数値計算は未実施（follow-up）" "sample-visual層は3-judge panelでなくオーケストレータ単発1パス。Chrome の「Apple Events からの JavaScript を許可」がデフォルト無効なためスクロール不可、hero/nav部分のみ視認（cards/grid/listセクション未視認）" "この macOS 環境は多数の並行 Claude Code セッションがフォーカスを奪い合うため（computer-use skill既知ハザード）、キー入力操作を避けAppleScriptのapp-scriptingのみに限定した" "kotoba-ui judge3体中1体がStructuredOutput retry cap超過で失敗（n=2で集計）" "サンプルは3種類・1画面構成（Team Dashboard相当）のみ、light-mode表示は未検証"], :adr/closing-summary-2026-07-13 "Closed at user's 'closing' instruction. Final state: 6 pages ever audited by this\n  system (4 samples + kami-studio + kami-creative-studio) = 100.00/100, 0 findings.\n  6 repos landed real merged fixes on their own main (kotoba-ui, liquid-glass-ui,\n  kami-studio, kami-creative-studio, plus 2 manifest/west.yml pin advances in\n  com-junkawasaki/root). 3 real tool bugs found and self-caught before shipping: (1)\n  heuristic-hypothesis doesn't verify selectors against real page markup -- UNFIXED,\n  top priority for a future session (it proposed a dead no-op CSS rule once, caught by\n  hand before shipping). (2) design-quality.audit's single-string API silently\n  undercounted pages with externally-linked CSS -- FIXED via score-site (addendum-d).\n  (3) tap-targets/focus-visible structurally false-positive on client-rendered SPAs --\n  documented as a standing limitation, not fixed. Open backlog for next session, in\n  priority order: fix heuristic-hypothesis's selector-verification gap; add a real\n  WCAG 1.4.3 contrast-ratio axis (seeded 3 iterations running); formalize/fix the CSR\n  blind spot; make :sample-visual a real 3-judge panel (currently single-pass); decide\n  whether to register kami-studio/kami-creative-studio in manifest/west.yml (left out\n  of scope deliberately).", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607132300: kotoba-lang design-system (uikit/appkit/kotoba-ui/liquid-glass-ui) UI/UX 品質を EDN で数値化する design-quality-score システムを導入する", :adr/source-format "edn"}]